# This is the control. The loop mentions `out` and lets it escape, so `out` counts as escaped before the versions of the loop are built, and nothing is assumed about it in the generic version.
# Fault injection, testing=IgnoreLoopEscapes: loops are assumed to mention no value from before the loop.
# `out` then stays fresh in the generic version, but what arrives there says otherwise, so the output stays correct.
